k00pa wrote:
> I found great strategy. First find wand of polymorph, zap shopkeeper
> (and hope it turns to easy enemy) then kill it, no penalties. Then use
> shop as stash where you but all your stuff. Easy way to rob shop also.

There arise a few questions with that approach... The "hope" factor
is _pure gambling_, so not appropriate if you want to win the game.
Then, what is the advantage compared to an ordinary room? You may
have the auto-rebuilt of digged shop walls in mind. This is slightly
better than an ordinary room but no guarantee; mind that monsters
can still slip through, and they can still be generated in shops in
the first place. In summary; the setup is a risk I would not suggest
to take, ordinary stashes are easy to built up, chests and boxes
and the E-word is effective and can be installed quite everywhere
in the dungeon. Also Sokoban is a guaranteed standard location to
deposit your items; on top of the E-word and hidden under a boulder.

